    // sequence (out/turn/alongside/home, the boat only) now starts there. The yacht's own timeline (her slow approach and hold, the zoom-in, where the camera aims) stays on `yacht` below.
    out: [0.70, 0.735],      // leg 1: comes in from the RIGHT-HAND edge, low in frame, heading west, aiming for her starboard quarter
    turn: [0.735, 0.77],     // leg 2: wide right-hand curve round onto her course
    yacht: { out: [0.58, 0.64], turn: [0.64, 0.70], alongside: [0.70, 0.82] },   // (the yacht's, the zoom's and the camera's windows: unchanged from before this change)
    // 30 Sep 2026, Simon: "we can further 'slow down time'... during the zoomed in segment for pilot boarding"
